1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,571
Coach: Now practise bringing several contributions together.

2
00:00:02,571 --> 00:00:06,429
Coach: Use the current snapshot of the book-club discussion,

3
00:00:06,429 --> 00:00:08,572
Coach: after the explicit proposal check.

4
00:00:08,572 --> 00:00:15,000
Coach: Your job is to make the shared position clear enough for another person to respond.

5
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:21,429
Coach: You are not announcing a final plan or trying to repeat every sentence in order.

6
00:00:21,779 --> 00:00:26,065
Coach: The candidate links a brief example, pair discussion and sharing,

7
00:00:26,065 --> 00:00:31,636
Coach: with at least five minutes for club questions inside the thirty-minute total.

8
00:00:31,636 --> 00:00:33,779
Coach: The resource limits still apply.

9
00:00:33,779 --> 00:00:38,065
Coach: No exact stage lengths or demonstration leader have been settled,

10
00:00:38,065 --> 00:00:41,922
Coach: so those checks must not disappear from the summary.

11
00:00:42,272 --> 00:00:48,272
Coach: Maya supports the sequence if the example stays brief and the pair task remains.

12
00:00:48,272 --> 00:00:52,558
Coach: Noah supports starting with an example and keeping question time,

13
00:00:52,558 --> 00:00:58,558
Coach: but is not ready to agree to the full sequence before timing is checked.

14
00:00:58,558 --> 00:01:03,272
Coach: These are related positions, not identical signatures on a completed plan.

15
00:01:11,622 --> 00:01:15,479
Coach: Think about what a listener needs to know now.

16
00:01:15,479 --> 00:01:18,908
Coach: Name the candidate without making it sound adopted.

17
00:01:18,908 --> 00:01:23,622
Coach: Include the support and the reservation that affect the next decision.

18
00:01:23,622 --> 00:01:29,194
Coach: Then offer a relevant check, such as working out stage lengths including transitions,

19
00:01:29,194 --> 00:01:33,908
Coach: rather than asking a vague question about whether everyone is happy.

20
00:01:34,258 --> 00:01:38,972
Coach: You may speak in English or make a few private notes.

21
00:01:38,972 --> 00:01:40,687
Coach: Nothing is recorded here.

22
00:01:40,687 --> 00:01:47,115
Coach: Leave out a detail only when it does not change the meaning of the proposal

23
00:01:47,115 --> 00:01:48,830
Coach: or a person's position.

24
00:01:48,830 --> 00:01:53,544
Coach: In particular, do not lose the words that make support conditional.

25
00:01:53,894 --> 00:01:58,180
Coach: You do not have to sound like a formal chairperson.

26
00:01:58,180 --> 00:02:01,608
Coach: A short, clear summary can invite a correction

27
00:02:01,608 --> 00:02:04,608
Coach: and leave another person room to continue.

28
00:02:04,608 --> 00:02:11,037
Coach: Choose ordinary wording that you could explain if someone asked what you meant by agreed,

29
00:02:11,037 --> 00:02:12,751
Coach: supported or still open.

30
00:02:13,101 --> 00:02:15,672
Coach: Take time to prepare your version.

31
00:02:15,672 --> 00:02:19,530
Coach: In Watch, a possible model follows the preparation pause.

32
00:02:19,530 --> 00:02:22,530
Coach: In Practice, continue when you are ready,

33
00:02:22,530 --> 00:02:26,815
Coach: look at the model if useful, or skip this rehearsal.

34
00:02:26,815 --> 00:02:29,815
Coach: The model will be a separate example,

35
00:02:29,815 --> 00:02:34,101
Coach: not a reply to words you may have said privately.

36
00:03:09,451 --> 00:03:13,737
You: Our candidate links a brief example, pair discussion and sharing,

37
00:03:13,737 --> 00:03:18,451
You: with at least five minutes for club questions inside thirty minutes.

38
00:03:18,451 --> 00:03:23,594
You: Maya supports the sequence if the example stays brief and pairs remain.

39
00:03:23,594 --> 00:03:26,594
You: Noah supports the example and question time,

40
00:03:26,594 --> 00:03:31,308
You: but wants the timings checked before agreeing to the whole sequence.

41
00:03:31,308 --> 00:03:34,737
You: Could we check a complete schedule, including transitions,

42
00:03:34,737 --> 00:03:37,308
You: and who would give the example?

43
00:03:37,658 --> 00:03:40,229
Noah: Please keep my timing question open.

44
00:03:40,229 --> 00:03:43,658
Noah: I haven't agreed to the full sequence yet.

45
00:03:44,008 --> 00:03:49,580
Coach: The model connects the elements, reports the two support statements with their limits,

46
00:03:49,580 --> 00:03:51,294
Coach: and offers a check.

47
00:03:51,294 --> 00:03:54,294
Coach: Noah's reply reinforces the open timing point.

48
00:03:54,294 --> 00:03:59,008
Coach: Nothing here adopts a schedule or proves the activity will work.

49
00:03:59,008 --> 00:04:03,294
Coach: You can use different wording while keeping those distinctions clear.

50
00:04:03,644 --> 00:04:07,073
Coach: Use the source statements to review any summary,

51
00:04:07,073 --> 00:04:11,358
Coach: whether you rehearsed one, watched the model or moved on.

52
00:04:11,358 --> 00:04:14,787
Coach: Does it distinguish the candidate from a decision?

53
00:04:14,787 --> 00:04:18,216
Coach: Does it keep each person's condition or reservation?

54
00:04:18,216 --> 00:04:22,930
Coach: Is the proposed next check still presented as something to discuss,

55
00:04:22,930 --> 00:04:25,930
Coach: rather than an assigned or completed action?

56
00:04:26,280 --> 00:04:30,137
Coach: If a phrase is too broad, revise that phrase.

57
00:04:30,137 --> 00:04:36,566
Coach: For example, replace everyone agrees with a more specific account of who supports which part.

58
00:04:36,566 --> 00:04:39,566
Coach: If your wording is accurate but long,

59
00:04:39,566 --> 00:04:42,566
Coach: shorten the repetition rather than the condition.

60
00:04:42,566 --> 00:04:48,566
Coach: The useful target is a clearer account, not a memorised version of the model.

61
00:05:00,916 --> 00:05:05,202
Coach: A summary can help the group see its next decision,

62
00:05:05,202 --> 00:05:09,059
Coach: but it does not make that decision for them.

63
00:05:09,059 --> 00:05:10,773
Coach: After offering a check,

64
00:05:10,773 --> 00:05:15,916
Coach: allow an answer and use the actual reply to update your account.

65
00:05:15,916 --> 00:05:20,630
Coach: Someone may qualify their support, disagree or ask for more information.

66
00:05:20,980 --> 00:05:24,409
Coach: For your next discussion, choose one small focus:

67
00:05:24,409 --> 00:05:29,980
Coach: keep a condition beside its supported element, separate a proposal from a decision,

68
00:05:29,980 --> 00:05:32,551
Coach: or name the next unresolved check.

69
00:05:32,551 --> 00:05:36,837
Coach: Choose the one that would help your own summaries most.

70
00:05:36,837 --> 00:05:43,694
Coach: The final section uses a different task to see what these distinctions still help you notice.
